{"name":"Centaur","hex":"#90673f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Centaur","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The constellation and zodiacal sign Sagittarius."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of centaur."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Centaur"}],"entries":[{"title":"Centaur","blocks":[{"text":"A centaur, occasionally hippocentaur, collectively called the Centaurs or the Ixionidae, is a creature from Greek mythology with the upper body of a human and the lower body and legs of a horse that was said to live in the mountains of Thessaly. In one version of the myth, the centaurs were named after Centaurus, and, through his brother Lapithes, were kin to the legendary tribe of the Lapiths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Terracotta_lekythos_%28oil_flask%29_with_centaur_battling_a_warrior_MET_DP161810.jpg/330px-Terracotta_lekythos_%28oil_flask%29_with_centaur_battling_a_warrior_MET_DP161810.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centaur"},{"title":"Centaur (rocket stage)","blocks":[{"text":"The Centaur is a family of rocket-propelled upper stages that has been in use since 1962. It is currently produced by United Launch Alliance (ULA) in two main versions. The 3.05 m (10 ft) diameter Centaur III (also known as the Common Centaur) serves as the second stage of the retiring Atlas V rocket, and the 5.4 m (17.7 ft) diameter Centaur V is used as the second stage of the Vulcan Centaur rocket. Centaur was the first rocket stage to use hydrolox propellant—liquid hydrogen (LH2) and liquid oxygen (LOX)—a high-energy combination well suited for upper stages but difficult to handle because both propellants must be stored at extremely low cryogenic temperatures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Landsat-9_Centaur_1_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Landsat-9_Centaur_1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centaur_(rocket_stage)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Foundry_Painter_ARV_402_22_Lapiths_fighting_centaurs_%2801%29.jpg/500px-Foundry_Painter_ARV_402_22_Lapiths_fighting_centaurs_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Foundry_Painter_ARV_402_22_Lapiths_fighting_centaurs_%2801%29.jpg/1280px-Foundry_Painter_ARV_402_22_Lapiths_fighting_centaurs_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Foundry_Painter_ARV_402_22_Lapiths_fighting_centaurs_%2801%29.jpg/500px-Foundry_Painter_ARV_402_22_Lapiths_fighting_centaurs_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Centauromachy, tondo of an Attic red-figure kylix, c. 480 BC","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFoundry_Painter_ARV_402_22_Lapiths_fighting_centaurs_(01).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Ac_marbles.jpg/500px-Ac_marbles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Ac_marbles.jpg/500px-Ac_marbles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Centaur in battle with a Lapith, on South Metope 31 of the Parthenon, c. 447–438 BC[9]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAc_marbles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Centaur_lifting_a_rock%2C_Attic_red-figured_kylix%2C_by_the_Bonn_Painter%2C_510-500_BC%2C_inv._16514_-_Museo_Gregoriano_Etrusco_-_Vatican_Museums_-_DSC01053.jpg/500px-Centaur_lifting_a_rock%2C_Attic_red-figured_kylix%2C_by_the_Bonn_Painter%2C_510-500_BC%2C_inv.